    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>First pregnancy at 38 (elderly primigravida), single live intrauterine pregnancy dated by ultrasound at 7 weeks 1 day</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O09.519</td><td>S — Synthetic modern prenatal care anchored to the documented report that she was pregnant when she died; the pregnancy itself is questioned in one source (CLM-0019).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Nausea and vomiting of pregnancy, moderate (PUQE-24 score 10), with early weight loss, under evaluation for hyperemesis gravidarum</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O21.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the hyperemesis gravidarum diagnosis at the sick visit; her documented &quot;perpetual nausea&quot; is D and the hyperemesis reading of it is R.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

